			<div class="content" id="post-content-4583429">
									

<p>First skip I've written in over three years, this one's about the US government finding and looting Atlantis.</p>
<p>To start with, some crit credits. A lot of people glanced at this, so if I forgot your name, let me know:</p>
<ul>
<li>Conwell</li>
<li>TyGently</li>
<li>Taffeta</li>
<li>tawny</li>
<li>A Random Day</li>
<li>ch00bakka</li>
<li>Anorrack</li>
<li>minathewitch</li>
</ul>
<p>Second, some NOTES:</p>
<ul>
<li>The list of missing superweapons here is meant to serve as a potential hook for future articles (skips, tales, goi formats), not unlike the Little Misters list. My hope is to eventually build a much larger and more detailed view of <tt>AQUARIAN DISCO</tt> and their history by offering snippets in each superweapon article, and in the process also provide a look at some of the political and diplomatic interactions that go on behind the Veil. If you're interested in taking a stab at one of these, hit me up.</li>
<li>There's more to the containment here than just the blockade, but the Foundation isn't privy to all of the details of the GOC's activities.</li>
<li>SCPS <em>Jump Jacked</em> and <em>Lunatic Leap</em> (as well as <em>Daring Dash</em>) are all clandestine aircraft carriers and submarine tenders &#8212; they look like normal civilian ships, but can hold one or two submarines in internal holds, and carry a few wings of aircraft. The GOC vessels are straight-up warships, probably comparable to a light cruiser.</li>
</ul>

							</div>

								
